+---
+id: dl-003-input-validation-for-title-priority-and-tags-lives-in-the-domain-as-a-new-invalid-input-result-error
+type: decision-log
+title: "Input validation for title, priority and tags lives in the domain, as a new invalid-input Result error"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Some screens pass whatever the user typed straight to `TaskList` without checking it first, so a
+blank title, a title far longer than any UI would reasonably show, a priority that is not one of the
+three the app knows, or a tag with a space in it (which would break tag-based filtering and display)
+could all end up stored. The fix had to work no matter which screen calls in, which rules out
+validating only in `src/index.ts` or in the app: it has to sit where `add`, `rename` and `tag` are
+actually implemented, in `src/domain/list.ts`, so every caller goes through it.
+
+## Decision
+
+Validation lives in a new `src/domain/validation.ts`, as three small functions —
+`validateTitle`, `validatePriority`, `validateTag` — each returning a `Result` rather than throwing,
+per `r4-errors-as-result`. They read the clock or randomness nowhere, satisfying `r3` and
+`determinism`. Rules, matching the request exactly: a title is invalid when empty or only spaces after
+trimming, or longer than 120 characters (checked after trimming, consistent with `createTask` already
+trimming the title it stores); a priority, when given, is invalid unless it is one of the `PRIORITIES`
+already declared in `task.ts`; a tag is invalid when it is the empty string or contains a space
+(checked on the raw string — tags are not trimmed elsewhere in the domain, so trimming here would be
+inconsistent with how `addTag`/`removeTag` compare tags).
+
+`TodoErrorCode` gains a fourth value, `invalid-input`, alongside `not-found`, `duplicate` and
+`invalid-state`, so callers that already switch on `error.code` get a new case to handle rather than a
+misclassified one.
+
+`list.add` validates the title, the priority and every tag in the input, in that order, before
+checking for a duplicate title or touching the id counter or the map. `list.rename` validates the new
+title before resolving `titleOrId`. `list.tag` validates the tag before resolving `titleOrId`. In every
+case the function returns the validation error immediately, so a rejected call leaves the list exactly
+as it was — no partial state, no advanced counter, no stored task.
+
+`list.untag` is deliberately not validated: removing a tag that would itself be invalid is harmless
+(it is simply not present, so nothing changes), and the request only asked to reject invalid input when
+a task is "added, renamed, or tagged".
+
+## Consequences
+
+- `add`, `rename` and `tag` can now return an `invalid-input` error in addition to the errors they
+  already returned; any caller that pattern-matches on `TodoErrorCode` exhaustively (e.g. a `switch`
+  with no `default`) needs a new case.
+- The 120-character and "no space in a tag" limits are hard-coded in `validation.ts` rather than
+  configurable; revisit if a future screen needs a different limit.
+- Validation runs before the duplicate-title check in `add` and before resolving `titleOrId` in
+  `rename`/`tag`, so an invalid title/tag is reported as `invalid-input` even when the target task does
+  not exist or the title would also collide; acceptable since the input is wrong regardless of what
+  else is true.
