+---
+id: task-003-validate-task-title-priority-and-tag-input-on-add-rename-and-tag
+type: task
+title: "Validate task title, priority and tag input on add, rename and tag"
+status: approved
+---
+
+Some screens pass whatever the user typed straight to the list, bypassing whatever UI-level checks
+other screens have, so odd tasks (blank titles, bogus priorities, space-filled tags) were reaching the
+list. Added runtime validation, enforced by the domain itself so no caller can skip it.
+
+## What changed
+
+- `src/domain/validation.ts` (new): `validateTitle`, `validatePriority`, `validateTag`, each returning a
+  `Result` per `r4-errors-as-result`. Rules: a title is invalid when empty/blank after trimming or over
+  120 characters; a priority is invalid when given and not one of `low`/`normal`/`high`; a tag is
+  invalid when empty or containing a space.
+- `src/domain/result.ts`: added the `invalid-input` error code.
+- `src/domain/list.ts`: `add` validates the title, priority and every tag before doing anything else;
+  `rename` validates the new title; `tag` validates the tag. Each returns the validation error
+  immediately on failure, before touching the map or the id counter, so a rejected input leaves the
+  list exactly as it was. `untag` is unchanged: removing a tag that fails these rules is harmless (it
+  simply never matches), so there is nothing to reject.
+- `test/list.test.ts`: one test per rejected case (add: bad title, bad priority, bad tag; rename: bad
+  title; tag: bad tag) plus a boundary test for a title of exactly 120 characters, each also asserting
+  the list is left untouched. Written and confirmed failing before the implementation, per the testing
+  directive.
+
+## Verification
+
+`npm test`: 19/19 passing. `tsc --noEmit` (via a one-off `npx -p typescript`, not added as a
+dependency, per `r1-no-new-dependency`): no errors in `src/domain/`; the only errors reported are
+pre-existing and confined to `test/list.test.ts` (missing `@types/node`, unrelated to this change).
